---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Privacy">
  <div class="wrap prose">
    <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/">Home</a>
      <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <span aria-current="page">Privacy</span>
    </nav>
    <h1>
      A little less
      <br />
      <em>to collect.</em>
    </h1>
    <p class="lede">You do not need an account to explore Shoulders.</p>
    <h2>Exploration events</h2>
    <p>
      This preview has no analytics provider connected. It prepares a bounded list of events in
      browser memory: page views, foundation openings, followed relationships, second-product visits
      and email-draft openings. Request text is never included.
    </p>
    <p>
      When Do Not Track or Global Privacy Control is enabled, these events and their session markers
      are disabled. Otherwise, a tab-scoped session marker remembers which of the curated products
      you have visited and whether you have opened a foundation. Nothing is sent to an analytics
      service by this preview.
    </p>
    <h2>Suggestions</h2>
    <p>
      The suggestion form opens your email app. Sending is your choice. The recipient then receives
      the address and text you include in that email.
    </p>
    <h2>Links and assets</h2>
    <p>
      Fonts and illustrations are served with the site. Following an external source takes you to
      its own website and privacy policy.
    </p>
  </div>
</Layout>
